# Using the Avalonia docs connector

Full write-up: `.claude/skills/avalonia-docs-connector/SKILL.md`.

An Avalonia MCP connector is configured. Before writing or editing any `.axaml`,
custom control, style selector or binding, call `get_avalonia_expert_rules` once
per session, then `search_avalonia_docs` for the topic. (If the connector is not
available in your Cursor session, fall back to the reference assemblies and the
submodule sources below.)

This project is on **Avalonia 12.1.1** — verify anything version-sensitive
rather than assuming 11.x. The Android lifetime change (see `project-overview`
known gaps) is exactly that mistake, and `AvaloniaMainActivity` went from generic
to non-generic in 12.

- `search_avalonia_docs` is more reliable than `lookup_avalonia_api`, which has
  gaps (no entry for `InputPane`, which `PresenterUserControl` relies on).
- The docs cover **stock Avalonia only**. `AvaloniaFramework` types
  (`VTextBoxWithLabel`, `PresenterBase`, `NavigationController`,
  `SynchronizedCommand`) are absent — read `external/AvaloniaFramework` or that
  repo's `README.md`.
- Some API details are faster to confirm against the reference assemblies at
  `~/.nuget/packages/avalonia/12.1.1/ref/net10.0/` than through the docs.
- The migration tools (`analyze_wpf_project`, `migrate_to_avalonia`,
  `migrate_to_xpf`, `lookup_wpf_to_avalonia_mapping`) are for WPF ports and are
  not relevant here.

Related: `styling-design-canvas` (the theme tokens, canvas and controls you will
be authoring against).
